# ALFRED point-in-time cache (#119). NOT committed: each vintage file carries the series' ENTIRE
# history (PAYEMS back to 1939), so a few hundred releases is ~12 MB of near-duplicate JSON. ALFRED
# vintages are immutable, so this buys speed, not integrity. The EVIDENCE is committed instead, as
# alfred_revision_<series>.csv — one row per release with the TradingView value, the first print, the
# current value and the shifted-month control, which is what anyone would actually want to check.
subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/alfred_cache/
!subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/alfred_revision_*.csv

# H1-B/H1-C server run logs (#115). Committed as EVIDENCE, like the perf logs: these are the raw
# console output of the two server runs whose every number is cited in the report, and the "LOCAL is
# the source of truth" rule means a server-only artefact does not count as recorded.
!subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/h1bc_run_*.log

# ...and the Phase 2 pre-registration artefacts (#116). phase2_pairs.csv IS the pre-registration: it
# fixes which 643 pairs Phase 2 is allowed to test and at what alpha. It was caught by the blanket
# *.csv rule and existed on ONE MACHINE ONLY, while I had already described it as "committed" and
# "machine-checkable" — the exact #94 inversion where a deliverable lives locally and vanishes from the
# repo. Worse than the earnings case, because a pre-registration that can be silently regenerated
# differently is not a pre-registration at all. The S2 probe verdicts are here for the same reason:
# which pairs are UNANSWERABLE is part of the record, not a working note.
!subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/phase2_pairs.csv
!subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/phase2_s2_probe.csv
!subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/phase2_s3_results.csv
!subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/phase2_s4_results.csv
!subprojects/Parametric-Indicators/optimize/fundamentals/api_eia_mechanism.csv

